# How long a browser may keep the website's static files (polish audit X12, 2026-10-04).
#
# Without this file every static file left the edge as "public, max-age=0, must-revalidate"
# (Cloudflare's default for Workers Static Assets), so a second page view asked the server about
# every font, stylesheet, script and photo again. The font answer arrived after ~112 ms, past
# `font-display: optional`'s ~100 ms window, and Chrome then refused the real font for the whole
# page (the D11 finding: body text drawn in Arial 60 times out of 60).
#
# Next's build output under /_next/static/ is content-hashed: a changed file gets a new name, so a
# year with `immutable` is safe (OpenNext for Cloudflare, "Caching"). The photo folders keep fixed
# names, so they get a week; a replaced photo reaches a returning visitor within seven days.
#
# ⚠️ NO `/*` RULE. Rules that both match are COMBINED, not overridden: a `/*` Cache-Control would
# be appended to every rule below and ship two contradictory values (.claude/rules/viewer-headers.md).
# src/staticHeaders.test.ts reads this file and fails on that.

/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/factory/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/families/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/standards/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/film/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

# Each page type's share picture (polish X14). Fixed names, like the photos: a remade card reaches a
# returning visitor within the week, and `scripts/gen-share-images.mjs` remakes them only on purpose.
/share/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
